R-FL15 R-E2 R-E4 R-J1 R-J2 (slice 262a, Design Q642, UX14, Q262-2, Q262-9): a flag given more than once on one line is a usage failure, exit 2, `flag '<flag>' is given more than once`, for a flag with a value, a global flag, --registry and --file (last-wins before), the = form; the flag whose second use comes first is named. A flag that is not for the command wins (Q262-9). With --json the envelope is on stdout and the line on stderr. The only Fx call is args (the parse fails before the environment). The list flags --ignore and --target stay repeatable (L0, ArgsTest).
